    "created_at": "2016-08-15T10:21:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-15T10:21:19Z",
    "body": "Sometimes two objects reference the same opaque origin. Those would be considered same-origin under this definition. When you calculate the origin of a URL, and it becomes an opaque origin, that opaque origin will always be unique. But that doesn't mean that an opaque origin cannot be shared.\n",
